---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import StatusBadge from "../components/StatusBadge.astro";
import { SUPPORT_URL } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base title="About — deckport" current="about">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose ab" style="max-width:820px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">about</p>
      <h2>What deckport is — and isn't</h2>
      <p class="ab-lead">
        Getting a loose, non-Steam game onto a Steam Deck and into Game Mode is
        more fiddly than it should be: copy it over, restore the execute bit the
        transfer stripped, register it by editing a binary file Steam guards, then
        hunt down artwork and name it by an app ID Steam computes internally. For
        self-contained native-Linux games — Godot, LÖVE, generic ELF — every bit of
        that is automatable. <strong>deckport automates it.</strong>
      </p>

      <h3>The honesty stance</h3>
      <div class="callout">
        <p class="label">built for the fun of it</p>
        <p style="margin:0;">
          The <code>shortcuts.vdf</code> reader/writer is tested for clean
          round-trips and byte-identical idempotent rewrites, and the
          deterministic-ID + artwork-naming approach is the same one shipping tools
          rely on. But the full chain hasn't been confirmed on real Deck hardware
          end to end yet — so seed recipes start at <code>unverified</code> or
          <code>needs-test</code>, and nothing is marked
          <span class="green">working</span> until a real Deck says so.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:1.1rem;">
        How a recipe earns its status — and the one line only real hardware crosses:
      </p>
      <div class="statusflow" aria-label="Recipe status lifecycle">
        <div class="sf-node">
          <StatusBadge status="unverified" />
          <p>auto-generated or guessed — never run</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-arrow">
          <span class="sf-g">→</span>
          <span>structure checked</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-node">
          <StatusBadge status="needs-test" />
          <p>engine, binary &amp; data files verified — but not launched</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-arrow sf-gate">
          <span class="sf-g">→</span>
          <span>only a real Deck test crosses this</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-node sf-earned">
          <StatusBadge status="working" />
          <p>ran on a real Deck — the SteamOS build is recorded in <code>verified_on</code></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size:.9rem;">
        And the honest dead-end:
        <StatusBadge status="borked" />
        means someone confirmed it does <em>not</em> run, with notes on why — just
        as useful as a success.
      </p>

      <h3>Non-goals</h3>
      <ul class="nope">
        <li><strong>Not</strong> a Wine/Proton prefix manager — that's Lutris and Bottles; deckport hands off.</li>
        <li><strong>Not</strong> a game store, downloader, or anything that distributes game files.</li>
        <li><strong>Not</strong> a DRM-circumvention tool — recipes describe prefix config only.</li>
        <li><strong>Not</strong> a heavyweight GUI launcher — the value is in being small and scriptable.</li>
        <li><strong>Not</strong> dependent on a running server — the CLI works fully offline.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Credits</h3>
      <ul class="credits">
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/SteamGridDB/steam-rom-manager" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><strong>Steam ROM Manager</strong></a>,{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/sonic2kk/steamtinkerlaunch" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><strong>SteamTinkerLaunch</strong></a>{" "}
          — the deterministic-app-ID pattern for shortcuts and artwork.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://lutris.net" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><strong>Lutris</strong></a>,{" "}
          <a href="https://usebottles.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><strong>Bottles</strong></a>,{" "}
          <a href="https://heroicgameslauncher.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><strong>Heroic</strong></a>{" "}
          — the mature way to run Windows games via Wine/Proton.
        </li>
        <li><a href="https://www.protondb.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><strong>ProtonDB</strong></a> — crowdsourced Proton compatibility data.</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.steamgriddb.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><strong>SteamGridDB</strong></a> — the artwork source.</li>
        <li><strong>VAPOR</strong> — the SteamGridDB artwork engine the fetcher is built from.</li>
      </ul>

      {
        SUPPORT_URL && (
          <div class="support-card">
            <h3>☕ Support deckport</h3>
            <p>
              This is a free, no-ads side project — config-only recipes, real
              artwork, no game files. If a recipe saved you an evening of fiddling
              and you feel like chipping in toward the hosting and the late-night
              fact-checking, it's appreciated. Entirely optional.
            </p>
            <a class="btn primary" href={SUPPORT_URL} rel="noopener" target="_blank">
              Buy me a coffee ↗
            </a>
          </div>
        )
      }

      <p class="note">
        Code is MIT; recipe data is open (CC0/CC-BY). Not affiliated with Valve.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .ab-lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .green { color: var(--green); }

  /* section headers with amber accent bar */
  .ab h3 {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0.9rem;
    padding-left: 0.7rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--amber);
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .callout {
    margin: 1.1rem 0;
  }

  /* status lifecycle flow — horizontal, stacks on mobile */
  .statusflow {
    display: flex;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 0.9rem 0;
  }
  .sf-node {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--panel);
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .sf-node p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--sub);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  /* the earned state — green */
  .sf-earned {
    border-color: var(--green);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--green) 7%, transparent);
  }
  .sf-arrow {
    flex: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    max-width: 5.5rem;
  }
  .sf-g {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--amber);
  }
  .sf-arrow > span:last-child {
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    color: var(--sub);
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  /* the gate to "working" — only a real Deck crosses it */
  .sf-gate .sf-g,
  .sf-gate > span:last-child {
    color: var(--green);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .statusflow {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.4rem;
    }
    .sf-arrow {
      flex-direction: row;
      max-width: none;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
    .sf-g {
      transform: rotate(90deg);
    }
  }

  /* non-goals — red ✕ markers */
  .nope {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .nope li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.9rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .nope li::before {
    content: "✕";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    color: var(--red);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .nope strong {
    color: var(--red);
  }

  /* credits — amber names, divided rows */
  .credits {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .credits li {
    padding: 0.6rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--sub);
  }
  .credits li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .credits strong {
    color: var(--amber);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
